# =============================================================================
# SUBMISSION AND PUBLISHING WORKSPACE — local-only, deliberately.
#
# These are the working files of *making* a hackathon submission, not of the
# product: the engineering notebook, the Devpost copy, the self-scored rubric,
# the release checklist, the film's script/storyboard/media manifest, the
# article evidence notes and the Builder Center publishing steps. None of them
# is needed to build, run, test, understand or judge Pool, and a public
# repository that carries them describes the workstation rather than the
# software. Kept on disk, kept out of git — the same treatment as AGENTS.md.
#
# What a judge needs instead is committed: README.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md,
# the two architecture diagrams, docs/AGENT_TRACE_EVIDENCE.md, and the film
# itself at the public submission link.
# =============================================================================
/BUILD_HISTORY.md
/docs/ARTICLE_NOTES.md
/docs/DEMO_SCRIPT.md
/docs/DEVPOST_DRAFT.md
/docs/FINAL_EXPERIENCE_PLAN.md
/docs/HACKATHON_SCORECARD.md
/docs/IMPECCABLE_HANDOFF.md
/docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md
/docs/VIDEO_*.md
/docs/builder-center-final/PUBLISHING_CHECKLIST.md
/docs/DEMO_POLISH_AUDIT.md
# Re-drives the four Builder Center captures and audits navigation. Article-production
# tooling by the same rule as the rest of this section — and it cannot run from a clean
# clone anyway: it resolves Playwright out of video/, which is not in this repository.
/scripts/audit_demo_polish.mjs

# =============================================================================
# VIDEO PRODUCTION — the entire tree is local-only, deliberately.
#
# video/ is a 12 GB production workspace across eleven cut directories: 1.6 GB of raw
# camera recordings, 71,627 derived PNG/JPEG frames, 570 narration WAV chunks and
# takes, presenter frames, per-cut audit dumps, the take reviewer's working state,
# third-party audio, the scene code and renderer, and the delivered film itself.
# Measured, not estimated. None of it is needed to build, run, test, or judge Pool,
# and none of it is reproducible-by-clone in any useful sense.
#
# What a judge needs is the film at the public submission link, not its sources —
# the hackathon requires the video on YouTube or Vimeo, never in the repository.
#
# Two licensing notes, both of which this rule enforces:
#   - The raw recordings are irreplaceable. They are ignored, never deleted.
#   - The intro/outro audio is Pixabay Content License, which forbids redistributing
#     the file standalone, so it must never be committed. Provenance is recorded in
#     video/final-hybrid-human/intro/ASSETS.md.
#
# This is one directory rule on purpose. It replaced ~30 per-cut patterns that had to
# be extended by hand every time a new cut directory appeared, which is how two 2.2 GB
# working copies escaped the rules once already.
# =============================================================================
/video/

# Article-production artefacts: screenshots captured from a running app for the
# Builder Center pieces, and the tooling that captures them. The six images the three
# final articles actually embed are committed under docs/builder-center-final/images/;
# everything else a capture run produces is regenerable and local-only.
/docs/builder-center-final/captures/
/docs/screenshots/

# Scratch: research spikes, throwaway notes, and anything being drafted before it
# either becomes part of the project or is deleted. (`scratch/` itself is already
# covered under Local data, above.)
notes/
*.tmp
*.local.md
